Thomas Wesley Hinton wrote:
>
> I have a wand of create monster, if I zap it, do I get tó choose?

No.  You get a random monster and that is all.  If you have a ring of
conflict you can zap it, run to the door, and watch the monster and
the priest battle.  Enough cycles and the priest will be killed or
you wwill run out of charges on the wand.

> If I kill the priest myself, will Odin kill me? Will my own god be so pissed
> that I can't appease him again (say, by saccing that unicorn I have with me
> ;) )

Killing the priest will reduce your alignment, but if you are already
level 11 you have alignment to spare.  Killing the priest will not
anger Tyr, so there will be no need to appease.  Killing the priest
will delete your telepathy so you will need to work through that later.

Basically if this is the only altar before the Castle that will be
your only choice.  Seriously consider making it to Medusa before you
are certain there are no other altars.

The method: Priests stay at their altar, so do it remotely.  Dig away
one of the walls.  Stack the opened spaces with very many missile
weapons, rocks, worthless glass that you've identified, whatever will
do damage.  Stay at where the wall was and start throwing missles and
zapping wands like an arcade game.  This way the priest cannot come
to you and Odin will not zap you because his reach is the same as the
priest's.  Keep throwing and zapping until the priest is dead.  Then
start offering at the altar to convert it, bring your luck up, get a
couple of artifact weapons, and get your telepathy back.

